        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Synod of Chester, Battle of Chester\n- People: Æthelfrith of Northumbria, Selyf Sarffgadau, Cadwal Crysban\n- Places: Bangor-on-Dee, Powys, Gwynedd, Rhôs, Northumbria\n- Organizations: ecclesiastical community at Bangor-on-Dee\n\nFacts:\n- The Synod of Chester led directly to the Battle of Chester.\n- During the Battle of Chester, Æthelfrith of Northumbria appears to have attacked the ecclesiastical community at Bangor-on-Dee.\n- During the Battle of Chester, Æthelfrith of Northumbria seems to have killed the king of Powys and possibly the king of Gwynedd.\n- The Battle of Chester resulted in the deaths of Selyf Sarffgadau of Powys and Cadwal Crysban of Rhôs.",
